    "result": "Perfect! All the changes are in place. Let me create a final summary of the implementation:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval` as requested:\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**frai-core (SDK Support)**:\n- Enhanced `generateReport()` to accept an optional `thresholds` object\n- Thresholds automatically calculate pass/fail status and add `passed` boolean and `thresholds` array to reports\n- Updated markdown reporter to include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status\n- JSON reports automatically include threshold results\n\n**frai-cli (Command-line Interface)**:\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option to `frai eval` command (repeatable)\n- Implemented `parseThresholds()` function with:\n  - Format validation: `<metric>=<number>`\n  - Range validation: minimum must be between 0 and 1\n  - Dynamic metric discovery: validates against available metrics from evaluations\n  - Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations()`\n- Proper exit codes:\n  - 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds provided)\n  - 1 if any threshold fails\n  - 2 for usage errors (malformed threshold, unknown metric, out-of-range value)\n\n**Documentation**:\n- Updated README.md with threshold option documentation\n- Added SDK example showing threshold usage\n- Documented valid metric IDs and behavior\n\n### Test Results\nAll new threshold tests pass \u2713:\n- \"evaluates thresholds - all pass\" \u2713\n- \"evaluates thresholds - one fails\" \u2713\n- \"evaluates thresholds - null score fails\" \u2713\n\nThe 2 pre-existing test failures mentioned in the requirement remain unchanged (unrelated to this feature).\n\nThe implementation fully supports the requirements:\n- Multiple thresholds can be specified\n- Metrics with null scores fail their thresholds\n- Reports are written regardless of pass/fail status\n- Works with custom metrics via SDK\n- Full validation and error handling",
